We need to generate an assert statement that corresponds to that comment. The comment: "If the list is initially empty, then the result is null."

We need to refer to the result as \result. Need to refer to the initial emptiness condition: before the operation, the list is empty. The method poll() reads first node before any modifications; it calls unlinkFirst only if f != null. So the spec: if the list was empty initially (size == 0, or first == null), then \result == null.

We need to use \old to refer to the state before. So condition: \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null. Or \old(this.size()) == 0 => \result == null. Use publicly accessible observer methods: isEmpty() or size(). Both are public. So we can use this.isEmpty().

Thus assert: assert \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null;

